/*
------------------------------------------------------------
Problem    : Find the Index of the First Occurrence in a String
Platform   : LeetCode
Topic      : Strings
Difficulty : Easy

Problem:
Given two strings, `haystack` and `needle`, return the index
of the first occurrence of `needle` in `haystack`.

If `needle` does not exist in `haystack`, return -1.

Approach:
Traverse every possible starting position in `haystack`
where `needle` can fit.

For each starting position, compare the characters of
`needle` with the corresponding characters in `haystack`.
If all characters match, return the current index.

If no complete match is found after checking all valid
positions, return -1.

Why does this work?

A substring match can only begin at positions where enough
characters remain in `haystack`.

By comparing characters one by one, we verify whether
`needle` matches completely without creating any additional
strings.

Algorithm:
1. Handle the empty `needle` case.
2. Traverse every valid starting position.
3. Compare characters one by one.
4. If every character matches, return the starting index.
5. If no match exists, return -1.

Time Complexity : O((m - n + 1) × n)

Reason:
In the worst case, each possible starting position requires
comparing all characters of `needle`.

Space Complexity : O(1)

Reason:
No additional data structures are used.

------------------------------------------------------------
*/

class Solution {
public:
    int strStr(string haystack, string needle) {

        int haystackLength = haystack.size();
        int needleLength = needle.size();

        // An empty needle is always found at index 0.
        if (needleLength == 0) {
            return 0;
        }

        // Check every possible starting position.
        for (int startIndex = 0;
             startIndex <= haystackLength - needleLength;
             startIndex++) {

            int currentIndex = 0;

            // Compare characters one by one.
            while (currentIndex < needleLength &&
                   haystack[startIndex + currentIndex] ==
                   needle[currentIndex]) {

                currentIndex++;
            }

            // Entire needle matched.
            if (currentIndex == needleLength) {
                return startIndex;
            }
        }

        return -1;
    }
};
